<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanghyang Siksa Kandang Karesian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1518</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sanghyang Siksa Kandang Karesian is an Old Sundanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> dated 1518, from the Sunda Kingdom of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. Written as a book of instruction, it sets out religious duties, moral rules and the practical knowledge expected of different ranks and occupations, from rulers and priests to craftsmen and farmers. It is one of the most important sources for the society, religion and culture of pre-Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a>.</p></div>
